> On Oct 17, 2024, at 13:22, RFC Errata System =
<rfc-editor@rfc-editor.org> wrote:
>=20
> The following errata report has been rejected for RFC8446,
> "The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.3".
>=20
> --------------------------------------
> You may review the report below and at:
> https://www.rfc-editor.org/errata/eid6136
>=20
> --------------------------------------
> Status: Rejected
> Type: Technical
>=20
> Reported by: Ben Smyth <research@bensmyth.com>
> Date Reported: 2020-04-28
> Rejected by: Paul Wouters (IESG)
>=20
> Section: 4.1.4
>=20
> Original Text
> -------------
>   Upon receipt of a HelloRetryRequest, the client MUST check the
>   legacy_version, legacy_session_id_echo, cipher_suite, and    =20
>   legacy_compression_method as specified in Section 4.1.3=20
>=20
> Corrected Text
> --------------
>=20
>=20
> Notes
> -----
> Section 4.1.3 defines no checks for legacy_version nor =
legacy_compression_method
> --VERIFIER NOTES--=20
>   It does have the listed fields and values it should contain (to =
check) in the previous 4.1.3 section.
>=20
> --------------------------------------
> RFC8446 (draft-ietf-tls-tls13-28)
> --------------------------------------
> Title               : The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol =
Version 1.3
